  "texts": {
    "preamble": "V.Subbaiah vs The Commissioner on 2 September, 2015 Author: M.Sathyanarayanan Bench: M.Sathyanarayanan In The High Court Of Judicature At Madras Dated: 02.09.2015 Coram: The Honourable Mr.Justice M.Sathyanarayanan W.P.No.27520 of 2015 V.Subbaiah .. Petitioner - Vs - 1. The Commissioner, Food Safety and Drug Administration, 359, Anna Salai, Chennai - 02. 2. The Director of Municipal Administration, Ezhilagam, Chepauk, Chennai - 5. ..",
    "facts": "2. The petitioner has entered the Municipal Service as Sanitary Inspector and subsequently he was given additional charge of Food Inspector from the year 2001 onwards and he would claim that he served to the satisfaction of his superior officers. It is further stated by the petitioner that he was falsely implicated in a criminal case in Cr.No.04/2009 and consequently, he was placed under suspension and subsequently it was revoked based on an order passed by this Court in W.P.No.34379 of 2014. 1 Based on which, the first respondent has invited list of candidates to fill up the post of Food Safety Officers. It is claimed by the petitioner that he has undergone training for Food Inspectors at King Institute, Guindy from 2001 onwards. Therefore, he made a representation dated 01.11.2014, to the first respondent praying for his absorption as Food Safety Officer in the existing vacancies.",
    "arguments": "The petitioner would further state that the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 came into being and the Food and Drug Administration Committee has recommended to create 199 post of Food Safety Officers in urban areas including Municipalities / Corporations. The grievance of the petitioner is that though the receipt of the representation has been acknowledged, no orders has been passed and hence he has come forward to file this writ petition.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "The petitioner would further state that the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 came into being and the Food and Drug Administration Committee has recommended to create 199 post of Food Safety Officers in urban areas including Municipalities / Corporations. The grievance of the petitioner is that though the receipt of the representation has been acknowledged, no orders has been passed and hence he has come forward to file this writ petition.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
